                <pb facs="0688" n="680" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg680"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5123/35: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-04T20:00:00-05:00">February 4, 1937—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>28. Your 53, February 2, 2 p.m., and 56, February 3, 2 p.m., in regard to income
                    tax. The Department approves your circularizing American consular offices in
                    China in the sense indicated in paragraphs 4 and 6 of telegram No. 53.</p>
                <p>The Department also approves the attitude and procedure outlined in the last
                    sentence of telegram 56.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
